KMSDRM: SDL_KMSDRM_ALL_DISPLAYS opts out of the drmConn filter

The drmConn patch registers only the connector EmulationStation chose, so
a dual-screen app never sees the second panel.  With the hint (or the
environment variable) set, every connected connector becomes a display.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-10-07 01:29:43.931022561 +0000
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-10-07 01:29:43.943022556 +0000
@@ -1177,11 +1177,17 @@
     }
     //
 
+    /* SDL_KMSDRM_ALL_DISPLAYS: every connected connector, not only the
+       drmConn one (dual-screen apps such as DSperate's dual-window mode) */
+    if (SDL_GetHintBoolean("SDL_KMSDRM_ALL_DISPLAYS", SDL_FALSE)) {
+        drmConn = -1;
+    }
+
     /* Iterate on the available connectors. For every connected connector,
        we create an SDL_Display and add it to the list of SDL Displays. */
     for (i = 0; i < resources->count_connectors; i++) {
         drmModeConnector *connector;
-        if(i != drmConn) continue;
+        if(drmConn >= 0 && i != drmConn) continue;
             connector = KMSDRM_drmModeGetConnector(viddata->drm_fd,
                                                    resources->connectors[i]);
 
